(a) No person, referred to in this section as harvester, involved in loading and hauling stone, pulpwood, fill dirt, sand, rock, all minerals and construction material or logging and timber operations shall not use an existing driveway or access point nor shall install any new driveway, temporary driveway, or means of ingress and egress to any property abutting a county road or county maintained road, without first making application to the board of commissioners through its code compliance officer for and receiving of a permit authorizing such installation or use.
